# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / cargo build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo's normalised manifest left behind by `cargo vendor` / unpacking
# vendored crates. The "real" manifest is the one without `.orig`.
*.orig
*.rej
# More `cargo vendor` artefacts inside the vendored revm-* crates. The
# workspace uses the root Cargo.lock; per-crate lockfiles inside a
# vendored crate are dead weight, and .cargo-ok / .cargo_vcs_info.json
# are extractor markers — none of these are load-bearing.
crates/revm-*/Cargo.lock
crates/revm-*/.cargo-ok
crates/revm-*/.cargo_vcs_info.json
# Coverage / profiling output
*.profraw
*.profdata
tarpaulin-report.*
coverage/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Toolchain shims set up by ./scripts/setup-libclang.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cargo/libclang-shim/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI tooling — deliberately NOT in the public repo. Covers per-tool
# state directories AND shared project-instruction files (CLAUDE.md,
# AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, etc.). If you want any of these locally,
# create them after cloning.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude*
CLAUDE.md
.cursor*
AGENTS.md
.aider*
.continue/
.github/copilot-*
.windsurfrules
.codeium/
.tabnine/
.cody/
.openhands/
.openai/
.gemini/
.copilot/
.devin/
.replit/
.zed/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS-generated cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets / credentials — defence in depth; nothing should match today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
secrets.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data — never commit chain state. Cheap to reproduce, expensive
# (and sometimes consensus-sensitive) to ship.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mainnet-data/
testnet-data/
nile-data/
shasta-data/
data/
db/
snapshots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local logs / debug dumps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
core
core.*
*.coredump

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference repositories cloned for grep / parity work. Not vendored — clone
# them yourself if you want them locally. See README's "Reference
# implementation" section.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
java-tron/
tronprotocol/
